[{:db/id "q-341671/field-1/192c6030d8816553cdfcf13c7f5f26bd0bc0f29788b453b1e64332880bc35044" :answer/id #uuid "76e7711b-030e-5e3e-bceb-b26a6febfd28" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341671/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "63ce6489-6b9c-5c3e-8c95-d580615b8b68" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-341671/field-1/192c6030d8816553cdfcf13c7f5f26bd0bc0f29788b453b1e64332880bc35044" :answer-field/choices ["q-341671/field-1/192c6030d8816553cdfcf13c7f5f26bd0bc0f29788b453b1e64332880bc35044"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-341671" :question/id #uuid "06e078d9-14de-5fbb-a951-fa0bc181f2a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-341671" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=ln⁡(9x)$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf=ln⁡u,\\,u=9x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=9.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot 9 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9x}\\cdot 9 \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{9x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{9}}{\\cancel{9}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-341671/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4ac7f7e-1e07-57d7-a82a-d6545588c2de"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-341671"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-341679/field-1/e95f75fcd2c377f651cdbba383f9037c0174ab5c7833c8c8583fcae14f1a8067" :answer/id #uuid "f51a9b49-6cac-5136-93b7-a9e6cef0db65" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{11}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341679/field-1/e83a540f3a0c82b4093cb3e2952b7e4cf1d91fdf67a578cdd4c22a4f9debc7d4" :answer/id #uuid "6cecb1c6-3a1b-5e2f-a84b-92cc6c13b85d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{11}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341679/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "c391a1e2-4765-5821-997f-8890f733fbdd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-341679/field-1/e95f75fcd2c377f651cdbba383f9037c0174ab5c7833c8c8583fcae14f1a8067" :answer-field/choices ["q-341679/field-1/e95f75fcd2c377f651cdbba383f9037c0174ab5c7833c8c8583fcae14f1a8067" "q-341679/field-1/e83a540f3a0c82b4093cb3e2952b7e4cf1d91fdf67a578cdd4c22a4f9debc7d4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-341679" :question/id #uuid "0bdbe537-8874-525b-aec8-402f441a2044" :question/math-academy-id "q-341679" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Find the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve $f(x)=ln⁡(7-4x)$ at the point where $x=-1.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf=ln⁡u,\\,u=7-4x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-4.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7-4x}\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{7-4x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of the tangent line at the point where $x=-1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}m=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{x=-1} & ={-\\frac{4}{7-4x}|}_{x=-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{7-4(-1)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{11}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-341679/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4ac7f7e-1e07-57d7-a82a-d6545588c2de"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-341679"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-48654/selection/f523fa367adf27890e17568ed32da30b3f640e17258d6f070b1338addf69e87e" :answer/id #uuid "72b54718-47fa-5ecf-b59c-ff07fb52defb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=x-4+4ln⁡8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48654/selection/74f0890d4193df0b1e37930854ec75f6ff50c088f11a4fa185b3251af82c62c8" :answer/id #uuid "888b24f5-922e-5da1-9fe7-915713648e78" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=x+4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48654/selection/f2adfea2e735434d319593db9ed92225eed16fcf264feab67dcbdf82977c87f4" :answer/id #uuid "5f9a34a7-e7c8-51bc-abf6-fa620ea60b53" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=2x-2-ln⁡8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48654/selection/35d786bf1f47c77933749b3796136a51172e4d412ae789d9f245e4b52c09327a" :answer/id #uuid "4afe095d-9ec2-5c11-b7ea-db9e85245279" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=x-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48654/selection/6b431dacd2c23ef3e9108a557dfeb859e1294802bcfe538961a170bb44c535ab" :answer/id #uuid "931a5bef-9c6a-582a-bcc7-c4d22079bfbf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=2x-8+4ln⁡8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48654/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "974c0400-857b-5e50-86e0-c7b746a19e63" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-48654/selection/f523fa367adf27890e17568ed32da30b3f640e17258d6f070b1338addf69e87e" :answer-field/choices ["q-48654/selection/f523fa367adf27890e17568ed32da30b3f640e17258d6f070b1338addf69e87e" "q-48654/selection/74f0890d4193df0b1e37930854ec75f6ff50c088f11a4fa185b3251af82c62c8" "q-48654/selection/f2adfea2e735434d319593db9ed92225eed16fcf264feab67dcbdf82977c87f4" "q-48654/selection/35d786bf1f47c77933749b3796136a51172e4d412ae789d9f245e4b52c09327a" "q-48654/selection/6b431dacd2c23ef3e9108a557dfeb859e1294802bcfe538961a170bb44c535ab"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-48654" :question/id #uuid "3f656447-8d86-5249-b18f-c8a1f82e6f4b" :question/math-academy-id "q-48654" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $f(x)=4ln⁡(2x)$ at the point $(4,4ln⁡8).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf=4ln⁡u,\\,u=2x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{4}{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{u}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{2x}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{2x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{2}\\cdot 4}{\\cancel{2}\\cdot x} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of the tangent line at the point where $x=4$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=4} & ={\\frac{4}{x}|}_{x=4}=\\frac{4}{4}=1\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the slope of the tangent line at the point $(4,4ln⁡8)$ is $m=1.$ Now, we find the equation of the tangent at that point:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-4ln⁡(8) & =1(x-4) \\\\ y & =x-4+4ln⁡(8)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-48654/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4ac7f7e-1e07-57d7-a82a-d6545588c2de"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-48654"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-310144/field-1/4eff627bd1b3f5f17c1fe8d52784e86b05fe5f910c8dd024a3cd97eeee1ae133" :answer/id #uuid "0cefcefd-ab4a-54a9-96ec-7fd9e98ed060" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{10}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-310144/field-1/5b6a7457ecf38e757655a8ab80cd7dca24376644ed8b5d929a23fb6af65f88f0" :answer/id #uuid "58f78de1-bf51-5725-9729-7397ef887e04" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-310144/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "422c0e8e-ef2d-54e8-8efc-86f338261860" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-310144/field-1/4eff627bd1b3f5f17c1fe8d52784e86b05fe5f910c8dd024a3cd97eeee1ae133" :answer-field/choices ["q-310144/field-1/4eff627bd1b3f5f17c1fe8d52784e86b05fe5f910c8dd024a3cd97eeee1ae133" "q-310144/field-1/5b6a7457ecf38e757655a8ab80cd7dca24376644ed8b5d929a23fb6af65f88f0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-310144" :question/id #uuid "5e3a8905-5d05-5bb6-8944-85d54da6c418" :question/math-academy-id "q-310144" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Find the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve $f(x)=ln⁡(5{x}^{2}+4)$ at the point where $x=1.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf=ln⁡u,\\,u=5{x}^{2}+4.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=10x.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot 10x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5{x}^{2}+4}\\cdot 10x \\\\  & =\\frac{10x}{5{x}^{2}+4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of the tangent line at the point where $x=1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}m=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{x=1} & ={\\frac{10x}{5{x}^{2}+4}|}_{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{10(1)}{5({1}^{2})+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{9}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-310144/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4ac7f7e-1e07-57d7-a82a-d6545588c2de"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-310144"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-11930/selection/7deae7978e85107833c8d9062127ab0636576ae05a8c60b0f7190df07317d0bf" :answer/id #uuid "0e9251de-e419-5ed8-ba64-a036e960f360" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11930/selection/0c88da4e67a916c1efb286eca3cbbf791695b5efb4a38c72d2e22c1b3e21d39e" :answer/id #uuid "25e41065-6d6b-538a-ad1b-fb38e2eee773" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8ln⁡8x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11930/selection/a222630b14700ef82a9661b504738af53626f11b528e05ea7aba64da55c1228d" :answer/id #uuid "8e5ffcab-1f74-5214-85ea-a1b0c723d37a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{ln⁡8x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11930/selection/b8a29b6527ccf08d8eb0ab65802ec04effaeb185cbdd73385e9dfdddbfa629fe" :answer/id #uuid "bd8a9a64-8ad0-5872-84f5-3dbf2a524064" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11930/selection/192c6030d8816553cdfcf13c7f5f26bd0bc0f29788b453b1e64332880bc35044" :answer/id #uuid "f2b4388f-43b9-5120-8829-4b2ac903498c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11930/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "748d2ad4-fbef-5ce7-b05a-18ced597c487" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-11930/selection/192c6030d8816553cdfcf13c7f5f26bd0bc0f29788b453b1e64332880bc35044" :answer-field/choices ["q-11930/selection/7deae7978e85107833c8d9062127ab0636576ae05a8c60b0f7190df07317d0bf" "q-11930/selection/0c88da4e67a916c1efb286eca3cbbf791695b5efb4a38c72d2e22c1b3e21d39e" "q-11930/selection/a222630b14700ef82a9661b504738af53626f11b528e05ea7aba64da55c1228d" "q-11930/selection/b8a29b6527ccf08d8eb0ab65802ec04effaeb185cbdd73385e9dfdddbfa629fe" "q-11930/selection/192c6030d8816553cdfcf13c7f5f26bd0bc0f29788b453b1e64332880bc35044"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-11930" :question/id #uuid "69a22f33-b1f5-5ce0-9f9a-c8a43f68878e" :question/math-academy-id "q-11930" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=ln⁡(8x)$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "Here $f(x)=ln⁡(8x)$ is a function of a function. We use the chain rule.First, we express $g(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf=ln⁡u,\\,u=8x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=8.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8x}\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{8x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{8}}{\\cancel{8}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-11930/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4ac7f7e-1e07-57d7-a82a-d6545588c2de"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-11930"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-48656/selection/4d95fef914abc76895d12bbc60868bc45d3cf5455c6e5ff54e91f2ab856c382a" :answer/id #uuid "cf9fc477-708c-5f22-bf99-c6cfa9d179d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3ln⁡(3)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48656/selection/b766c652a44789b64f79006393af5cd49605d3ed436123bd2874d8b848b232c8" :answer/id #uuid "75b89287-4684-5719-bd1e-e17a7b3b5803" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{ln⁡(3)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48656/selection/a26d5438abcb61c44aedae7d88ac0709a49a62dfbfc2b3b8ab3adc6742043b48" :answer/id #uuid "c544ccdd-2aaf-5acd-a2ee-d0ef9deba832" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5ln⁡(3)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48656/selection/c50d3e6934484c179f2848197702e120ce5e80c1d8d42c7595ff0700c3f5ee85" :answer/id #uuid "d3ef1960-6b71-5262-95bd-60b544bab73e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{15}{ln⁡(3)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48656/selection/8bf71bea1eabf18d30cc86b92695fbc01f86e749a176ca56e2a4aedbb39b6119" :answer/id #uuid "538c641b-ef04-5b24-91f4-4bdb3aae5979" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{ln⁡(3)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48656/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b98b6051-6b87-5677-8d65-c3dac87def85" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-48656/selection/c50d3e6934484c179f2848197702e120ce5e80c1d8d42c7595ff0700c3f5ee85" :answer-field/choices ["q-48656/selection/4d95fef914abc76895d12bbc60868bc45d3cf5455c6e5ff54e91f2ab856c382a" "q-48656/selection/b766c652a44789b64f79006393af5cd49605d3ed436123bd2874d8b848b232c8" "q-48656/selection/a26d5438abcb61c44aedae7d88ac0709a49a62dfbfc2b3b8ab3adc6742043b48" "q-48656/selection/c50d3e6934484c179f2848197702e120ce5e80c1d8d42c7595ff0700c3f5ee85" "q-48656/selection/8bf71bea1eabf18d30cc86b92695fbc01f86e749a176ca56e2a4aedbb39b6119"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-48656" :question/id #uuid "d30a7821-a43d-5a20-b43b-a88de1758226" :question/math-academy-id "q-48656" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Find the slope of the tangent to the curve $y={log}_{3}⁡(5x-2)+5$ at the point where $x=\\frac{7}{15}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny={log}_{3}⁡(u)+5,\\,u=5x-2.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{uln⁡(3)},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=5.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{uln⁡(3)}\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(5x-2)ln⁡(3)}\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{(5x-2)ln⁡(3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of the tangent line at the point where $x=\\frac{7}{15}$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}m=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{x=7/15} & =\\frac{5}{(5x-2)ln⁡(3)}{|}_{x=7/15} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{(5(\\frac{7}{15})-2)ln⁡(3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{\\frac{1}{3}ln⁡(3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{ln⁡(3)}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-48656/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a9102c1c-1c38-58dd-9932-b04bd24a6846"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-48656"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-341691/field-1/7937134982b294009cd3a84328efea1d67b9607d6cd8bde9b7cf23025869716d" :answer/id #uuid "4dafbfec-c1a7-5ce8-84d6-4984fb3f1394" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{x\\ln(6)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341691/field-1/ae8f8573805b559d44a6f4ae32c25ba3112387d2542d48a8307b65c5c0bc1d7c" :answer/id #uuid "7146ea97-87ff-56d7-94f0-6daf91862074" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x\\ln(6)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341691/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "bf1029b5-4090-506c-9b0b-049fd97904d5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-341691/field-1/7937134982b294009cd3a84328efea1d67b9607d6cd8bde9b7cf23025869716d" :answer-field/choices ["q-341691/field-1/7937134982b294009cd3a84328efea1d67b9607d6cd8bde9b7cf23025869716d" "q-341691/field-1/ae8f8573805b559d44a6f4ae32c25ba3112387d2542d48a8307b65c5c0bc1d7c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-341691" :question/id #uuid "9016a16d-888e-5ccf-8278-30b6de2dd539" :question/math-academy-id "q-341691" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Given that $y={log}_{6}⁡(-3{x}^{3}),$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ in terms of $x.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny={log}_{6}⁡(u),\\,u=-3{x}^{3}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{uln⁡(6)},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-9{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{uln⁡(6)}\\cdot (-9{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{-9{x}^{2}}{-3{x}^{3}ln⁡(6)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{-3{x}^{2}}\\cdot 3}{\\cancel{-3{x}^{2}}\\cdot xln⁡(6)} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{xln⁡(6)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-341691/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a9102c1c-1c38-58dd-9932-b04bd24a6846"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-341691"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-71478/selection/98224ef965df24365a761a2940915b9c83a3d15993a8295eb523cd3da74f4d58" :answer/id #uuid "cb1c4470-59a5-56a6-b16d-9eb3c32646be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{xln⁡(3)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71478/selection/202ab40b8630f31a9b3a085e3c37da9b82d7f6b9c89c3d152d3277988a48dd1f" :answer/id #uuid "b4d0ce7b-c8ae-5ca5-b0cc-3e7afa91688c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71478/selection/c3067c0bca497e0c738be51ac4fffa3d0182ec1d728b917fd4a6e75dd1509dac" :answer/id #uuid "bc4ad5c5-0f08-555e-bc16-9c770278830b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2xln⁡(3)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71478/selection/19518834b4a9e5a6805b91623b182c569ba80d44c2f0e29cff81194ed1214532" :answer/id #uuid "184df436-4da1-5c0f-96a3-0e3deafe1be3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71478/selection/c99ec127d3373db3e16dd45667a8538ee92c7acd1f7e2e9fba9cb0ad5bba4c80" :answer/id #uuid "7cfa62c2-8a78-5aed-bd86-2fbb168fcce8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{xln⁡(3)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71478/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f51f6fbd-5372-5bf4-8e80-40eb6da4aff8" :answer-field/key "selection" :ans